\p
\v 36 \w And Abigail| strong="H26" \w* [came]{strong=“H935” x-morph=“strongMorph: \sc Th\sc*8799”} \w to Nabal| strong="H5037" \w*; [and, behold, he held a feast]{strong=“H4960”} \w in his house| strong="H1004" \w*, \w like the feast| strong="H4960" \w* \w of a king| strong="H4428" \w*; [and Nabal’s]{strong=“H5037”} \w heart| strong="H3820" \w* was \w merry| strong="H2896" \w* within him, for he was \w very| strong="H3966" \w* \w drunken| strong="H7910" \w*: [wherefore she told]{strong=“H5046” x-morph=“strongMorph: \sc Th\sc*8689”} \w him nothing| strong="H1697" \w*, \w less| strong="H6996" \w* \w or more| strong="H1419" \w*, \w until the morning| strong="H1242" \w* \w light| strong="H216" \w*. 
\v 37 \w But it came to pass in the morning| strong="H1242" \w*, \w when the wine| strong="H3196" \w* [was gone out]{strong=“H3318” x-morph=“strongMorph: \sc Th\sc*8800”} \w of Nabal| strong="H5037" \w*, \w and his wife| strong="H802" \w* [had told]{strong=“H5046” x-morph=“strongMorph: \sc Th\sc*8686”} \w him these things| strong="H1697" \w*, \w that his heart| strong="H3820" \w* [died]{strong=“H4191” x-morph=“strongMorph: \sc Th\sc*8799”} \w within| strong="H7130" \w* him, and he became as \w a stone| strong="H68" \w*. 
